---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { ChartCanvas, ChartComposition, ChartCredits, ChartOptions, ChartPlayground } from '../../components/ChartDemo';
import { BusinessCharts } from '../../components/BusinessChartsDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Chart"
  description="Ready charts for dashboards, from trends and bars to funnels, heatmaps, and flows, built on Recharts with themed series colors, tooltips, and legends."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Chart</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Draws usage over days and values across categories. Two ready charts cover the common cases;{' '}
    <code>ChartContainer</code> wraps any other Recharts chart with the same colors, tooltip, and legend.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="chart-demo">
    <ChartCredits client:load />
  </div>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Daily usage"
      code={`import { UsageChart, type UsageSeries } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chart";

const series: UsageSeries[] = [
  { key: "s0", label: "claude-sonnet-4.5", color: "var(--sprout-chart-1)" },
  { key: "s1", label: "gpt-5", color: "var(--sprout-chart-2)" },
  { key: "s2", label: "2 more", color: "var(--sprout-muted)" },
];

<UsageChart
  days={[
    { date: "2026-10-16", s0: 12.5, s1: 4, s2: 0.6 },
    { date: "2026-10-17", s0: 9, s1: null },
  ]}
  series={series}
/>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>UsageChart</code> stacks one bar per day, 256px tall. Each day is a row with a UTC <code>date</code> (
        <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>) and a value per series key. A missing or <code>null</code> value leaves that series out
        of the day’s tooltip. Day labels read like “Oct 17”;
        <code>locale</code> changes the language.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>CategoryChart</code> draws side-by-side bars per category with a legend, 288px tall. <code>category</code>{' '}
        names the row key that labels each group.
      </li>
      <li>
        Both take <code>title</code>, which names the chart for screen readers, and <code>className</code> to change the
        height.
      </li>
      <li>
        Series colors are any CSS color. The palette is
        <code>--sprout-chart-1</code> to <code>--sprout-chart-10</code>, with
        <code>--sprout-muted</code> for a folded “N more” series.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Business charts</h2>
    <p>
      Fifteen ready charts for dashboards. They share one data shape: <code>rows</code>, the <code>category</code> key
      that names each row, and
      <code>series</code> with a key, label, and color. All take
      <code>title</code>, <code>className</code>, and
      <code>valueFormatter</code> for axis ticks and tooltips.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <BusinessCharts client:load />
    </div>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Revenue by month"
      code={`import { TrendChart } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chart";

const usd = (value: number) =>
  value.toLocaleString("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD" });

<TrendChart
  rows={[
    { month: "Jan", subscriptions: 42000, services: 18000 },
    { month: "Feb", subscriptions: 46000, services: 17000 },
  ]}
  category="month"
  series={[
    { key: "subscriptions", label: "Subscriptions", color: "var(--sprout-chart-1)" },
    { key: "services", label: "Services", color: "var(--sprout-chart-2)" },
  ]}
  valueFormatter={usd}
  title="Revenue by month"
/>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Over time:</strong>
        <code>TrendChart</code> (lines;
        <code>curve</code> is smooth, linear, or step), <code>AreaTrendChart</code>(<code>stack</code> is none, stacked,
        or percent), and
        <code>Sparkline</code> (a 40px line for stat tiles).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Compare:</strong>
        <code>CategoryChart</code> takes
        <code>horizontal</code> and <code>stack</code>; negative values hang below a zero line. <code>ComboChart</code>{' '}
        mixes bars and lines; a series with
        <code>axis: "right"</code> gets its own scale and
        <code>rightValueFormatter</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shares:</strong>
        <code>DonutChart</code> (or
        <code>variant="pie"</code>) and <code>TreemapChart</code> take
        <code>rows</code>, <code>category</code>, and <code>value</code>. The top five parts get chart colors; the rest
        fold into one muted “N more” part.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Progress and flow:</strong>
        <code>GaugeChart</code> shows
        <code>value</code> of <code>max</code> as a meter.
        <code>StepFunnelChart</code> shows each step’s count and share of the first.
        <code>WaterfallChart</code> adds each step’s change to a running total; steps in <code>totals</code> stand on
        zero.
        <code>SankeyChart</code> takes <code>nodes</code> and
        <code>links</code> by index.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Patterns:</strong>
        <code>HeatmapChart</code> is a table of cells in five shades of one color.
        <code>TimelineChart</code> draws tasks from <code>start</code> to <code>end</code>, colored by
        <code>seriesKey</code>; a row with no end is a diamond. It ships from
        <code>@tulipfarm/sprout/timeline</code>; see <a href="/components/timeline/">Timeline</a> for windows and row
        actions. <code>ScatterPlotChart</code> plots
        <code>x</code> against <code>y</code>, with <code>size</code> for bubbles.
        <code>RadarScoreChart</code> compares scores on many axes.
      </li>
      <li>No chart shares a name with a Recharts export, so you can import both in one file.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Canvas results</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChartCanvas client:load />
    </div>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A chart canvas item"
      code={`import { CanvasSection } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/canvas";
import { CategoryChart } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chart";

<CanvasSection title={item.title}>
  <CategoryChart rows={content.rows} category={content.category} series={content.series} />
</CanvasSection>`}
    />
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Playground</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChartPlayground client:load />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Tooltip and legend</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChartOptions client:load />
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>ChartTooltipContent</code>: <code>indicator</code> is
        <code>"dot"</code> (default), <code>"line"</code>, or
        <code>"dashed"</code>. With one series and a line or dashed indicator, the label moves into the row.{' '}
        <code>hideLabel</code>,<code>hideIndicator</code>, <code>labelFormatter</code>,<code>labelClassName</code>,{' '}
        <code>formatter</code>,<code>color</code>, <code>nameKey</code>, and <code>labelKey</code>
        change what it shows.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>ChartLegendContent</code>: <code>hideIcon</code> shows swatches instead of config icons, and{' '}
        <code>nameKey</code> picks the config entry. On a top legend, the 12px gap moves below it.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Custom charts</h2>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ChartComposition client:load />
    </div>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="ChartContainer around a Recharts chart"
      code={`import { CartesianGrid, Line, LineChart, XAxis } from "recharts";
import {
  ChartContainer,
  ChartLegend,
  ChartLegendContent,
  ChartTooltip,
  ChartTooltipContent,
  chartColor,
  type ChartConfig,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/chart";

const config = {
  chats: { label: "Chats", theme: { light: "#245cba", dark: "#9cbdff" } },
  agentRuns: { label: "Agent runs", color: "var(--sprout-chart-4)" },
} satisfies ChartConfig;

<ChartContainer config={config} style={{ height: 256 }}>
  <LineChart data={weeks} accessibilityLayer title="Chats and agent runs by week">
    <CartesianGrid vertical={false} />
    <XAxis dataKey="week" tickLine={false} axisLine={false} />
    <ChartTooltip content={<ChartTooltipContent indicator="line" />} />
    <ChartLegend verticalAlign="top" itemSorter={null} content={<ChartLegendContent />} />
    <Line dataKey="chats" stroke={chartColor("chats")} dot={false} />
    <Line dataKey="agentRuns" stroke={chartColor("agentRuns")} dot={false} />
  </LineChart>
</ChartContainer>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>ChartContainer</code> is 16:9 unless you give it a height. It writes{' '}
      <code>--sprout-chart-color-&lt;key&gt;</code> for each config entry; <code>chartColor(key)</code> returns that
      variable. Entries with <code>theme</code> switch value in dark mode. <code>ChartStyle</code>
      is the style tag it renders. <code>ChartTooltip</code> and
      <code>ChartLegend</code> are Recharts’ <code>Tooltip</code> and
      <code>Legend</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The ready charts turn on Recharts’ accessibility layer. The chart is one tab stop, named by <code>title</code>.
      Left and Right arrow keys move the tooltip between days or categories, and a 2px focus ring shows. Keep the real
      numbers in text or a table next to the chart, as the credits page does.
    </p>
    <p>
      The tooltip moves in 160ms and stays still with reduced motion. Bars draw without animation. In forced colors, the
      tooltip is outlined and swatches keep their colors.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Series use <code>--sprout-chart-1</code> to
      <code>--sprout-chart-10</code>, with light and dark values. Each points at a named hue:{' '}
      <code>--sprout-indigo</code>, <code>--sprout-green</code>,<code>--sprout-orange</code>, <code>--sprout-red</code>,
      <code>--sprout-sky</code>, <code>--sprout-purple</code>,<code>--sprout-yellow</code>, <code>--sprout-teal</code>,
      <code>--sprout-blue</code>, and <code>--sprout-tan</code>. Tailwind gets them as <code>bg-sprout-chart-1</code>{' '}
      and <code>bg-sprout-green</code>
      and so on, for swatches beside a chart. Ticks use <code>--sprout-muted</code>, grid lines
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, the hover band <code>--sprout-hover</code>, and the tooltip{' '}
      <code>--sprout-surface</code> with
      <code>--sprout-line</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
